    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37066" root="كفأ" body-key="k">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَفَآءٌ</span></b>  (K) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَفَأءَةٌ</span></b>  (S, K) <i>Likeness;
equality.</i> (S, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَفَأءٌ</span> <i>A slight inclination,
to one side, of a camel's hump,</i> and the like.
This is the slightest of faults in a camel; for
when the camel grows fat, his hump becomes
erect. (TA.)

